      "message": "test(kernel): re-triage three port pins after the solidcore move\n\nThe pin move 55d0e76 -> 2016386 changed three kernel pins:\n\n- blend: the rim chamfer's default path now gives the cone (WR-421).\n  The \"not yet\" test becomes a passing pin: heal to a closed solid,\n  then the cone's closed form.\n- corrupt_input: a box at a NaN origin is now refused. Pin \"Err\".\n- import_corpus: the writer now prints the zone tolerance as 1e-5, so\n  the literal corpus edits changed nothing. Find the header line by its\n  label, assert that each edit changes the file, and name the refusal\n  text of a non-finite tolerance in a new test. All rows keep their pins.\n\nRefs #2781\nRefs #917\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
