        "date": "2026-11-19T20:04:19Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(kernel): refuse non-finite lift samples and tolerances in KernelTrims\n\nReview fixes for PR #2797:\n- lifts_onto refuses a lift sample whose distance is not finite\n  (f64::max dropped a NaN); unit test pins the refusal text.\n- trims refuses a face, edge or vertex tolerance that is not a finite\n  number of zero or more before any .max uses it.\n- The lift check holds a pcurve to min(held tolerance, MAX_EDGE_GAP_MM).\n- New inch-unit closed-form test on fillet_corner.step (edited in memory).\n- The off-face pin also asserts the face and edge parts of the text.\n- step_twisted_flank gate map says which fixtures reach KernelTrims; the\n  8000 mm3 derivation is in the test.\n- Decision file: Why moved before the bench, lift readings, #939 rows.\n- Hand-format the long Blend arms and corpus rows.\n\nRefs #2781\nRefs #917\nRefs #939\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
